# DB connection (shiny_reader role -- SELECT-only, see supabase/roles.sql).
# Use Supabase's Supavisor pooler in SESSION mode (port 5432) -- NOT the
# direct db.<ref>.supabase.co host (IPv6-only, most hosting has no IPv6
# egress -- this cost us a failed Render deploy, see the main README) and
# NOT transaction mode (port 6543, doesn't support everything a persistent
# app session needs). Get the exact hostname from Supabase Dashboard ->
# your project -> Connect -> Session pooler -- don't guess it, the
# aws-<N>-<region> prefix isn't predictable (we hit aws-0- when the real
# value was aws-1- for an otherwise-identical project). The username MUST
# include the project ref suffix -- "shiny_reader.<project-ref>", not just
# "shiny_reader" -- or Supavisor rejects it with a confusing
# "tenant/user not found" error that looks like a wrong password.
SUPABASE_DB_HOST=aws-N-your-region.pooler.supabase.com
SUPABASE_DB_PORT=5432
SUPABASE_DB_NAME=postgres
SUPABASE_DB_USER=shiny_reader.your-project-ref
SUPABASE_DB_PASSWORD=your_password_here

# Second, write-capable pool (shiny_editor role -- see supabase/roles.sql).
# Used only by the Survey Detail (fish edit), Project Tagging, and NEPS Tool
# Export/Import tabs -- everything else keeps using the read-only pool above.
# Same host/port/dbname as above, different role -- same username-suffix
# rule applies ("shiny_editor.<project-ref>", not just "shiny_editor").
SUPABASE_DB_EDITOR_USER=shiny_editor.your-project-ref
SUPABASE_DB_EDITOR_PASSWORD=your_password_here

# Used only by the QC & Photo Review tab to generate signed URLs for the
# private photo storage bucket (see R/fn_db_queries.R::sign_photo_url()).
SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY=your_service_key_here
STORAGE_BUCKET=ef-photos

# NOTE: .Renviron is NOT deployed automatically to shinyapps.io/Posit
# Connect -- these must also be set via that platform's own
# environment-variable configuration UI. See deploy.R.
